Hundreds of thousands of protesters are expected to march through French cities and public workers to strike on Thursday, in a fresh test for President Emmanuel Macron after weeks of ​unrest that have rattled ‌his government and dominated the agenda five months ahead of a presidential election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1182cb7c-d8df-11f1-837f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-063742-063927-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1182cb7c-d8df-11f1-837f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-063742-063927-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16619da8-d8df-11f1-9aa0-75828042d9f5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 06:24:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Live: France braces for nationwide strikes in fresh test for Macron’s policies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261105-live-france-nationwide-strikes-living-costs</link><description>
Strikes and demonstrations are planned across France on Thursday, with trade unions urging the government to support households struggling with rising living costs. The nationwide action follows weeks of social unrest. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1562138-d5f7-11f1-8cc8-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T212107Z-663067613-RC2FEOAZ2S8M-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1562138-d5f7-11f1-8cc8-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T212107Z-663067613-RC2FEOAZ2S8M-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63218ce8-d8c1-11f1-bba7-9fe13f883f11</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 05:53:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1562138-d5f7-11f1-8cc8-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T212107Z-663067613-RC2FEOAZ2S8M-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg">© Abdul Saboor, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Melania Trump to host Ukrainian, Russian officials at White House</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-melania-trump-to-host-ukrainian-russian-officials-at-white-house</link><description>
Delegations of Russian and Ukrainian officials, including human rights chiefs from both countries, are set to meet with US First Lady Melania Trump at the White House Thursday ahead of talks in Abu Dhabi aimed at ending the Ukraine war. It comes weeks after Melania Trump helped broker a partial ceasefire that enabled the evacuation of civilians from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/137d8a76-d8d9-11f1-a4b1-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2f7f2262d4da4497ef29903a2565b6f31f07f054.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/137d8a76-d8d9-11f1-a4b1-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2f7f2262d4da4497ef29903a2565b6f31f07f054.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">14b7cc80-d8d9-11f1-bab8-c5769b69bd0c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 05:23:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/137d8a76-d8d9-11f1-a4b1-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2f7f2262d4da4497ef29903a2565b6f31f07f054.jpg">© Iryna Rybakova, AFP via handout </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong gets 10 more years in jail for foreign collusion</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-joshua-wong-hong-kong-10-years-jail-foreign-collusion</link><description>
Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in prison on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, a court summary said. Wong, 30, pleaded guilty in September to seeking foreign sanctions against Hong Kong and China under Beijing’s national security law, having spent nearly six years imprisoned.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bac80546-d89c-11f1-8ab0-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/a3febbc244aae5c0e71fa2e37cf9f5a49bf1acb0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bac80546-d89c-11f1-8ab0-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/a3febbc244aae5c0e71fa2e37cf9f5a49bf1acb0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16c3581a-d8c9-11f1-a120-9f5dcb84c312</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 03:31:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bac80546-d89c-11f1-8ab0-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/a3febbc244aae5c0e71fa2e37cf9f5a49bf1acb0.jpg">© Alastair Pike, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>South Korea to deploy military mission to keep Strait of Hormuz open</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-south-korea-military-mission-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
South Korea will deploy maritime patrol aircraft and an explosive ordnance disposal team near the Strait of Hormuz to help keep the waterway open, its defence ministry said Thursday. Seoul said it would protect commercial shipping and energy supplies while ruling out military intervention in the ongoing US-Iran war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0048f40-c016-11f1-b91d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/99ebe76c25b49d6da267803d0e58260a8db5112b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0048f40-c016-11f1-b91d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/99ebe76c25b49d6da267803d0e58260a8db5112b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f98789a8-d8bc-11f1-929a-db85ee62d1c5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 02:17:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0048f40-c016-11f1-b91d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/99ebe76c25b49d6da267803d0e58260a8db5112b.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Champions League: Real Madrid seal late comeback as Liverpool lose to Fenerbahce</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261104-champions-league-real-madrid-comeback-liverpool-fenerbahce</link><description>
Real Madrid maintained their perfect Champions League record as Federico Valverde’s stoppage-time strike secured a 3-2 comeback win at AEK Athens on Wednesday. Madrid twice trailed before Valverde scored from long range in the 92nd minute. Liverpool’s winning start ended with a surprise 3-2 defeat at Fenerbahce in the competition.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7394906c-d889-11f1-a2e1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/59cca8cf697732ef2e207385238d87640ec92383.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7394906c-d889-11f1-a2e1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/59cca8cf697732ef2e207385238d87640ec92383.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f820fa56-d89c-11f1-bf47-ef5e4f3caec0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 22:17:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7394906c-d889-11f1-a2e1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/59cca8cf697732ef2e207385238d87640ec92383.jpg">© Angelos Tzortzinis, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu claims 'serious concerns' of foreign spending to sway Israeli election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-netanyahu-claims-serious-concerns-of-foreign-spending-to-sway-israeli-election</link><description>
